<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The OAuth redirect scheme (ADR-0026, #137) is deliberately SHARED across all three build
	     configurations (Debug/ProdDebug/Release, ADR-0047): the redirect URI is registered server-side per
	     app, so a per-variant scheme would break sign-in on two of the three. The cost is that with
	     coexisting installs LaunchServices picks ONE of them arbitrarily to hand a redirect to — acceptable
	     because dev-PAT seeding (ADR-0012, the DevAccounts/DevStagingToken keys below) is how the two
	     debuggable variants sign in; only Release relies on the browser leg. -->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>com.circuitstitch.deferno.auth-redirect</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>com.circuitstitch.deferno</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>LSMultipleInstancesProhibited</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- Dev-only seeding (ADR-0012/0047), read by DefernoRoot.seedDevAccounts(). Both keys substitute a
	     DEFERNO_SEED_* **slot**, and nothing defines either slot by default — an undefined build setting
	     expands to empty, so the default for every configuration, present and future, is "seeds nothing".
	     A configuration opts in by mapping the slot to the secret that feeds it (project.yml
	     `settings.configs`, from the gitignored Local.xcconfig ← Secrets.xcconfig chain):

	       Debug      DEFERNO_SEED_STAGING_TOKEN = $(DEV_STAGING_TOKEN)   → a "Dev (staging)" Account
	       ProdDebug  DEFERNO_SEED_ACCOUNTS      = $(DEV_ACCOUNTS)        → the disposable prod Test Account
	       Release    (neither)                                           → nothing

	     ADR-0047's core safety property — a Production-env install can never seed a *staging* PAT — is
	     therefore what ProdDebug does NOT say, not a "" pin someone has to remember. DevAccounts is the
	     twin of Android's `deferno.prod.accounts` (a ';'-separated `id:label:token` list fed to
	     DevAccounts.from); seedDevAccounts() has always read the key, and ProdDebug is the first
	     configuration to populate it. Secrets.xcconfig's own key names are unchanged, so the file is
	     still byte-identical to the one app/iosApp reads. -->
	<key>DevStagingToken</key>
	<string>$(DEFERNO_SEED_STAGING_TOKEN)</string>
	<key>DevAccounts</key>
	<string>$(DEFERNO_SEED_ACCOUNTS)</string>
	<!-- The backend environment, injected per Xcode build configuration via the DEFERNO_ENV build setting
	     (ADR-0047). DefernoApp reads this and maps it to DefernoEnvironment, decoupling the env from the
	     debug/release build type (macOS used to derive it from `Platform.isDebugBinary`). -->
	<key>DefernoEnv</key>
	<string>$(DEFERNO_ENV)</string>
</dict>
</plist>
